diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index a45a290..bc29b0f 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -4,6 +4,10 @@
 
 The simulator uses MuJoCo to simulate individual workpieces landing against a conveyor belt and side wall. It estimates pose incidence, distinguishes settled and unsettled outcomes, and assesses how observed poses respond to disturbances. A PyQt6 GUI supports parameter studies and visible trials; the command line supports repeatable batches and assessment of saved results.
 
+For the verified Kl4i, Kf2a and Kf4i catalogue meshes, grouping retains persistent seated-energy minima and minimax-height paths: 60° local paths, 0.1° sampling and 0.5 mm escape barriers. Other unlisted meshes retain the legacy whole-group diameter guard and representative behavior.
+
+Kk2i, Kl2a and Kk4a use simpler rounded support families. Circumferential roll is ignored within the same extrusion-axis/support family; wide cut-feature supports remain distinct from the cylindrical tessellation strips. Axis alignment uses 10°, support-normal matching uses 5°, and a broad side facet has at least twice the median side-strip area. Kl2a's end-on-belt azimuths also merge. Kk4a retains signed axis directions, with tilted observations left separate for review. This rule does not claim that all merged orientations have a 0.5 mm energy barrier. Dispatch requires both the catalogue filename identity and its pinned STL SHA-256. Individual orientations, pose IDs, counts, recognition symmetry and tolerances remain unchanged, and incomplete disturbance assessments do not produce stability representatives.
+
 The Beckhoff benchmark ran on 7–8 November 2026 and covered **240,000 drops** across 12 workpieces, with 10,000 trials per workpiece in each belt mode.
 
 [User guide](USER_GUIDE.md) · [Windows launchers](WindowsLaunchers/README.md) · [Current GUI profile](configs/gui-current.json) · [Benchmark timing records](https://github.com/match-BiBaZu/BiBaZu_StableComponentenPoses/tree/4df4f1b27f928adca5e5d74377f8212c8f1ae0c9/timing/20261107_10000)
